{
  "title": "Scapulothoracic Dissociation",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/trauma/1014/scapulothoracic-dissociation",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 13 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Scapulothoracic Dissociation is a high-energy traumatic disruption of the scapulothoracic articulation often associated with severe neurovascular injuries, scapula fractures, and clavicular fractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made with the edge of the scapula being displaced > 1 cm from the spinous process as compared to the contralateral side. CT scan of the chest will show an asymmetric distance from the spinous process to the medial edge of the scapular body.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally open reduction and internal fixation of associated fractures and urgent exploration in the setting of vascular injuries. Functional outcome is dependent on the level of neurologic injury.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually caused by a **lateral traction injury** to the shoulder girdle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "involves significant trauma to heart, chest wall and lungs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "orthopaedic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "scapula fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "clavicle fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "AC dislocation/separation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "sternoclavicular dislocation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**flail extremity** (52%)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "complete loss of motor and sensory function rendering the extremity non-functional",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "vascular injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**subclavian artery** most commonly injured",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "axillary artery",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurologic injury (up to 90%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ipsilateral brachial plexus injury (often complete)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "neurologic injuries more common than vascular injuries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Scapulothoracic joint",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "a sliding joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "articulates with ribs 2-7",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "moves into abduction at 2:1 ratio",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "GH joint 120°",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ST joint 60°",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Neurovascular anatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "brachial plexus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "subclavian artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1014/images/vasculature.jpg",
                  "caption": "Vasculature around shoulder"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "axillary artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1014/images/vasculature.jpg",
                  "caption": "Vasculature around shoulder"
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1014/images/axillary%20artery%20and%20branches.jpg",
                  "caption": "axillary a. and branches"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "history of high energy trauma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain in involved upper extremity (UE)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "numbness/tingling in involved UE",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "significant swelling in shoulder region",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "bruising around shoulder",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "vascular exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**decreased or absent pulses** in involved UE",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurological exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "neurologic deficits in UE",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "neurological status critical part of exam",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "required views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP chest",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "recommended view",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral of shoulder as tolerated",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "appropriate images of suspected fracture sites",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**laterally displaced scapula**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1014/images/xr%20std.jpg",
                      "caption": "Scapulothoracic dissociation"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "edge of scapula displaced > 1 cm from spinous process as compared to contralateral side",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "widely displaced clavicle fx",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "AC separation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "sternoclavicular dislocation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "chest CT",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "axial views",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "asymmetric distance from spinous process to medial edge of scapular body",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Angiogram",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indicated to detect injury to subclavian and axillary artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "immobilization/supportive care",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**patients without significant vascular injury who are hemodynamically stable**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "patients may have adequate collateral flow to UE even with injury",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "high lateral thoracotomy with vascular repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "axillary artery injury in hemodynamically unstable patient",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "median sternotomy with vascular repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "more proximal arterial injury (i.e., subclavian artery) in a hemodynamically unstable patient",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ORIF of the clavicle or AC joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "associated clavicle and AC injuries",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "forequarter amputation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "complete brachial plexus injury",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Mortality rate of 10%**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Functional outcome is dependent on **neurologic injury**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "if return of neurological function is unlikely, early amputation is recommended",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
